        "game.core.world.secret": {
          "status": "active",
          "summary": "Prepared, unplayed situation. Opening: at the next session Elowen Pike may ask Ganji why the noon bell rang thirteen times as the empty tax wagon entered Bramblebridge market. Goals: Elowen wants lawful humane tolls; Tibb wants a truthful report respected; Merrit wants safe hospitality and the burned-inn letters traced; Odo wants oral memory and hives preserved; Nan wants charters stabilized without exposing private conclusions. Unused scenes: rainy Gilded Kettle, rainy Weir Bridge toll approach, and North Bell Tower before noon. Clues concern dry flour, pulley fibers, a changed whistle, an altered alley map, and barge-signal timing. Success enables a witnessed lawful intervention; premature confrontation advances the carriers but leaves clearer tracks; delay changes the next signal while physical evidence remains. Optional hooks: a Mallow Abbey charter discrepancy and the Gilded Kettle letters remain separate unresolved threads.",
